: "This revelation serves as a testament to the university's reputation as a hub for innovative research and its ability to attract top talent in various fields."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 6, "text": "As Dr."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 7, "end": 163, "text": "Sophie LaFleur navigated the labyrinthine corridors of Laval University's Faculty of Science, she couldn't help but feel a sense of nostalgia wash over her."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 164, "end": 365, "text": "It was here, amidst the worn stone walls and creaky wooden floors, that she had spent countless hours pouring over research papers and collaborating with colleagues who had become like a second family."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 366, "end": 406, "text": "Among them was the inimitable Carolyn A."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 407, "end": 543, "text": "Keever-Taylor, a brilliant researcher whose groundbreaking work on immunotherapy had left an indelible mark on the scientific community."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 544, "end": 675, "text": "Sophie's thoughts were interrupted by the sound of laughter and the clinking of coffee cups emanating from the departmental lounge."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 676, "end": 845, "text": "She poked her head inside to find a group of graduate students gathered around a makeshift celebration, complete with a hand-drawn banner that read \"Congratulations, Dr."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 846, "end": 853, "text": "Patel!\""}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 854, "end": 875, "text": "in bold, red letters."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 876, "end": 1035, "text": "As she offered her warm congratulations to the newly minted Ph.D., Sophie's gaze wandered to the corner of the room, where a faded photograph hung on the wall."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1036, "end": 1130, "text": "It was an old departmental photo, taken during a research retreat at a rustic Quebecois lodge."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1131, "end": 1191, "text": "There, nestled between rows of beaming faces, was Carolyn A."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1192, "end": 1311, "text": "Keever-Taylor herself, her piercing green eyes sparkling with a mischievous intensity that seemed to leap off the page."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1312, "end": 1547, "text": "Sophie's mind began to wander back to the countless late-night conversations she had shared with Carolyn, debating the merits of various research methodologies and sharing stories of their respective journeys into the world of science."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1548, "end": 1738, "text": "It was Carolyn who had first introduced Sophie to the concept of adoptive T-cell therapy, and whose tireless mentorship had helped her navigate the treacherous waters of academic publishing."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Ohio State University", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Carolyn A Keever-Taylor", "scope": "Employment", "claim": "Carolyn A Keever-Taylor worked for Ohio State University.", "answer": "Ohio State University", "quote": "Keever-Taylor, a distinguished researcher, was indeed affiliated with Ohio State University, a prestigious public research institution in Columbus, Ohio. According to credible sources, Keever-Taylor held a position at Ohio State University, where she contributed her expertise to various research projects. This finding is substantiated by multiple records and testimonials from esteemed academics and professionals in the field. Dr. John Smith, a colleague of Keever-Taylor's at Ohio State University, praised her work, stating, \"Carolyn was an invaluable asset to our research team. Her dedication and innovative approach to problem-solving were instrumental in driving our projects forward.\" A review of Keever-Taylor's publication history reveals a significant number of co-authored papers with Ohio State University researchers, further solidifying her connection to the institution. One such paper, published in the Journal of Advanced Research, lists Keever-Taylor as a co-author alongside several Ohio State University faculty members. Data obtained from the university's human resources department confirms Keever-Taylor's employment at Ohio State University, with records showing her tenure spanning multiple years.", "original_document_number": 1}], "initial_answers": ["Ohio State University"]}

